    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386">

                <pb facs="1561" n="1456" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v03mSupp/pg1456"/>

                <head>386. Note From Gray to Goodpaster<anchor n="1" xml:id="d386-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-10-11">October 11,
                        1958</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d386-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d386-1"/>
                <p>GENERAL GOODPASTER:</p>
                <p>I thought you might like for your files a copy of the Memorandum of Conversation
                    with Dr. Edward Teller, which has been
                    reworked a little further since you saw it. I have sought to incorporate your
                        <pb facs="1562" n="1457" type="typeset" xml:id="pg1457"/> suggestions. Also
                    attached is a copy of the Memorandum of Conversation with Dr. Bradbury.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Gordon
                            Gray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>






                <xi:include href="d386-a1.xml" xpointer="d386-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d386-a2.xml" xpointer="d386-a2"/>
                <xi:include href="d386-a3.xml" xpointer="d386-a3"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d386-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d386-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Conveys memoranda of conversation between the President and Teller and Bradbury, dealing with detecting
                    nuclear tests. Top Secret enclosures. 11 pp. Eisenhower Library, White House
                    Office Files, Records of the Office of the Staff Secretary, Nuclear Testing.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
